---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const joinForm = Boolean(site.joinEndpoint);
---
<Legal title="Privacy Policy" description="What personal information the Larrikin Coffee Collective collects and why.">
  <p>
    This explains what personal information {site.name} ("we", "us") collects when you use our
    ordering app.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies of its own and has no analytics or advertising trackers.
    {joinForm
      ? 'It collects personal information only if you use the join form (described below).'
      : "It doesn't collect personal information."}
    The map in the Hubs section loads map data from <a href="https://openfreemap.org">OpenFreeMap</a>.
    Your browser connects to their servers to do that, so they can see your IP address. OpenFreeMap says
    it doesn't use cookies and its access logs don't contain IP addresses by default; see their
    <a href="https://openfreemap.org/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. We don't receive or store that
    information.
  </p>

  {joinForm && (
    <>
      <h2>The join form</h2>
      <p>
        If you use the join form, we collect the name, email address, nearest hub and (optionally)
        favourite way to drink coffee that you enter. We use them to set you up with the ordering app,
        invite you to our Discord, and reply to you. The form is handled by a Cloudflare Worker, which
        passes your answers to a private channel on our Discord server that only our team can see. We
        don't store them anywhere else. We delete your request from that channel once we've set you up,
        or sooner if you ask us to.
      </p>
      <p>
        To block bots, the form uses Cloudflare Turnstile. Cloudflare says it processes your IP address,
        TLS fingerprint, User-Agent header, and the website's key and origin for this; see
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/">Cloudflare's Turnstile privacy addendum</a>.
        The Turnstile check loads from Cloudflare only when you reach the join form.
      </p>
    </>
  )}

  <p>Everything else below is about the ordering app.</p>

  <h2>What we collect in the ordering app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your email address, and the name, phone number and pickup hub you give us.</li>
    <li><strong>Order history:</strong> the items you've ordered, order totals, and whether you've paid and picked up.</li>
    <li><strong>Email records:</strong> a log of the order and payment emails we send you, and whether sending succeeded.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    To run the group order: build the combined order, track payments, organise pickup, and email
    you about your orders. We don't sell your information or use it for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Who handles it</h2>
  <p>
    Admins of the app can see members' details, orders and payment status. Sign-in is handled by
    Cloudflare Access, and our email provider delivers the emails we send you. Our community chat
    runs on Discord, which handles what you share there under <a href="https://discord.com/privacy">its own privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Access and deletion</h2>
  <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete your information at any time.</p>

  {site.contactEmail && (
    <>
      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
    </>
  )}
</Legal>
